## Purpose

Close the V4 provider-schema/parser contradiction that previously allowed the Responses API schema to emit a passage kind that the local parser rejected.

V4 remains experimental and is not the default launcher.

## Changes

- add a strict V4 transport schema with separate structural slots:
  - summary -> `SYNTHESIS` only;
  - body -> `EXPLANATION | EXAMPLE | CONTRAST | BIFURCATION` only;
  - closing limits -> `LIMIT` only;
- route the experimental V4 app through that strict transport;
- remove the emergency role-kind canonicalization from the app path;
- keep deterministic known German/source-language normalization before parsing;
- malformed/replayed `kind` metadata is now preserved and rejected rather than repaired;
- add meta-tests proving every provider-allowed kind is accepted by the parser in the same slot and every known foreign kind is rejected.

## Why this is different from PR #219

#219 prevented the live crash by canonicalizing redundant metadata after the provider returned it. This PR removes the contradictory state from the provider contract itself and restores fail-closed parsing for malformed replay payloads.

## Boundaries

No P1, P2A, P2B, report-plan, renderer, archive or doctrine change. No clinical-quality claim. No user testing requested.

