Supersedes #729 after the original branch accumulated unrelated CI fixes and became non-mergeable.

## Threat
The frontend image uses build context `./frontend` and `COPY . .`, but that context had no `frontend/.dockerignore`. The repository-root `.dockerignore` does not protect a separate frontend build context, so local `frontend/.env` files, key/certificate files, or credential JSON could be sent to the Docker builder and copied into build stages.

## Fix
- add a frontend-context `.dockerignore` excluding local env files, key/certificate material, credential JSON, dependency/build trees, and scratch files;
- keep `.env.example` available as a narrow documentation exception;
- extend the canonical Secret scanning workflow with a fail-closed frontend Docker build-context policy check;
- assert that the frontend Dockerfile still performs the broad context copy the policy is protecting;
- require credential/key exclusions explicitly and reject unreviewed reinclusions;
- run the same policy from canonical quality gates and cover fail-closed cases with focused regressions.

## Clean rebuild
This replacement was rebuilt from current `main` and contains only the six intended Docker-secret-boundary files/edits. Unrelated CodeQL, workflow-input, and merge-readiness changes from the stale #729 branch are intentionally excluded.

